{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Moses would take the tent.</b> This is in the present tense, for he would do so regularly. And it says 'far from the camp' because he would distance himself from the camp of Israel, for they were like excommunicated ones from Heaven on account of the sin of the calf, and he would seek from an excommunicated one to the master, from an excommunicated one to the disciple." "<b>And everyone who sought HaShem would go out to the tent of meeting which was outside the camp.</b> This teaches you that the Shekhinah did not dwell within the camp. And the verse should properly have said 'everyone who sought Moses,' but from here we learn that Moses was called by the unique Name; and so we find that Jacob was called by the name El, as it says (Genesis 33:20): ״ויקרא לו אלהי ישראל״ — as I explained there; and so we find with the name of the righteous one, that she was called by the unique Name, as it is written (ibid. 25): ״ותלך לדרוש את ה׳״ and it is written (ibid.): ״ויאמר ה׳ לה״ — and our Sages of blessed memory interpreted it by means of a name, for the unique Name did not speak with her at all; and so we find with King Messiah that he is called by the unique Name, as it says (Jeremiah 23:6–7): ״וזה שמו אשר יקראו ה׳ צדקנו״; and likewise Jerusalem (Ezekiel 48:35): ״ושם העיר מיום ה׳ שמה״ — אל תקרי שמה אלא שמה, do not read 'its name' but rather 'its name [i.e., the name of HaShem]'; and the reason for all of them is that one who cleaves to a thing is called by the name of the thing to which he cleaves, and the agent is called by the name of the sender; and from this we find that the angels are called by the unique Name in places throughout Scripture, as it is written (Genesis 18:13): ״ויאמר ה׳ אל אברהם למה זה צחקה שרה״ — but this was an angel, and he was called by the unique Name, as I explained there; and likewise (ibid. 19): ״וה׳ המטיר״ — this is Gabriel according to our Sages of blessed memory; מאת ה׳ — from the Holy One, blessed be He." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'And Moses would take the tent and pitch it for himself outside the camp, far off' (וגו׳) — 'far off,' this is within bowshot, and its measure is a mil, in the manner of what is written (Joshua 3:4): ״אך רחוק יהיה ביניכם וביניו כאלפים אמה במדה״. 'And everyone who sought HaShem' — it is not written here 'everyone who sought Moses,' but rather 'everyone who sought HaShem'; from here they said: whoever receives the countenance of an elder is as though he receives the countenance of the Shekhinah, as it says: 'And everyone who sought HaShem' — even the angels and the seraphim seek Him, saying to one another: 'Behold, He is placed in the tent of Moses'; the sun and the moon seek Him, saying: 'Behold, He is placed in the tent of Moses.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:46.001318356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}